---
import StrikethroughPage from '../components/StrikethroughPage.astro';
---

<StrikethroughPage lang="en">
  <!-- Add / edit the English article content here. -->
  <article class="prose wrap max-w-[820px] mx-auto py-10">
    <h2>What is strikethrough text?</h2>
    <p>
      Strikethrough text has a line drawn through the middle of every letter, like this: s̶t̶r̶i̶k̶e̶t̶h̶r̶o̶u̶g̶h̶. It is used to show something is cancelled, corrected, joked about or no longer true.
    </p>
    <h2>How to use the strikethrough text generator</h2>
    <p>
      Type your text in the box, tap any style to see it in the live preview, then press Copy and paste it into your bio, caption, chat or comment. No app and no sign-up are needed.
    </p>
    <h2>Where can I paste it?</h2>
    <p>
      The result is made of Unicode characters, so it works on Instagram, WhatsApp, Discord, TikTok, Snapchat, X and most other places that accept text.
    </p>
  </article>
</StrikethroughPage>
